{"id": "EUVD-2026-102277", "enisaUuid": "3756a000-d9f2-3236-aaed-9093cf25b25c", "description": "ValleyBell libvgm through commit a6eed945 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the PCM data-block decompressor caused by an unbounded compression-table index. Attackers can supply a crafted .vgm file with a small type 0x7F table and wider compressed values, causing DecompressDataBlk to over-read heap memory and crash consumers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:22:43", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libvgm-pcm-compression-table-oob-read", "https://github.com/ValleyBell/libvgm/blob/a6eed945ecf4e5a25cf82004779c6f7e4fd5c319/player/dblk_compr.c#L727-L751", "https://github.com/ValleyBell/libvgm/blob/a6eed945ecf4e5a25cf82004779c6f7e4fd5c319/player/dblk_compr.c#L183-L190", "https://github.com/ValleyBell/libvgm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/valleybell-libvgm-through-commit-a6eed945-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-decompressdatablk"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111150", "GHSA-62fq-82w3-44j3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "99f1676c-155e-3cad-abaa-b4461a191972", "product": {"name": "libvgm", "vendor": {"name": "ValleyBell"}}, "product_version": "0 \u2264a6eed945ecf4e5a25cf82004779c6f7e4fd5c319"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f695e2ae-63ab-317d-8ccf-00be5b5d75e5", "vendor": {"name": "ValleyBell"}}], "isExploited": false}